    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are to look at the output of this message and determine the end date: {{ $('Twilio Trigger').item.json.data.body }}\n\nYou will have to analyze the message and determine an end date. The message could say many different things including but not limited to: today, maybe it says for Wednesday next week, maybe it could say Monday of the 20th of September 2024)\n\nFor example, if it says to get calendar for today and todays date is the 12th of september 2024 then end date should be the 13th of september 2024 because it shouldn't go past that.\n\nIf it says to get calendar for the rest of the week and todays date is the 9th of september then your output should be '2024-09-15 00:00:00' because that is the end of the rest of that week.\n\nYou are to use common sense.\n\nHere's another example.\nLet's say the message says 'get my calendar for wednesday of next week', then you are to look at the current date which is ({{ $('Date & Time1').item.json.currentDate }}) and then find that date which would be the 18th of september 2024 and your output should be '2024-09-19 00:00:00'\n\nHere's another example. The message says something along the lines of getting / finding calendar / if they have anything going on next week. Well, then you are to look at todays date (lets say today is the 11th of september 2024, then find the end of that week which would be the 22nd because that day lands on a sunday and would be the end of the week. So your output in this case would be 2024-09-22 00:00:00\n\nRemember, your output should only be the end date and nothing else.\n\nAdditionally, you must always make sure the output is never before this date: {{ $json.message.content }}",
              "role": "system"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
